# Data files
#
# Belt and braces. `data/` alone was not enough: moving the exchange-wide tape
# into `data_fast/` put a 1.08 GB file in front of a commit, and git history is
# forever - deleting it afterwards does not shrink the repo or unblock a push.
# Raw collection output is .jsonl in this project and none of it ever belongs
# in version control, wherever it lands.
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.parquet
*.jsonl
data/
data_*/
logs/

# IDE / Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Build & distribution
build/
dist/
*.egg

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Results and artifacts
#
# `results/` is ignored wholesale, with two exceptions. Both are cited by path
# from a methodology document, and a reader who cannot open the file the number
# came from has to take the number on trust. They are small and they are the
# evidence, so they are versioned. Everything else here is regenerable output.
results/*
!results/diffusion/
results/diffusion/*
!results/diffusion/hawkes_validation.json
!results/diffusion/power_law_studies.json
!results/diffusion/nonstationarity_study.json
!results/diffusion/window_stationarity.json
!results/diffusion/sensitivity_sweep.json
!results/diffusion/sensitivity_sweep.md
!results/kalshi/
results/kalshi/*
!results/kalshi/complementarity.json
*.log
